      "language": null,
      "description": "An attacker exploited two vulnerabilities in Fluidkey's self-hosted SigNoz logging infrastructure to access internal logs containing user session tokens. Using those tokens, the attacker created and approved fraudulent transfer requests and increased two-factor spending limits. When affected users unlocked their applications, the apps signed the prepared transfers, allowing approximately $1.6M to be stolen from 52 accounts across six chains. Users' private spending keys were not compromised"
